      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5f2f6f47cb5f2349c1873556|full_name}: \nI made a cyberpunk model.\nI added a mechanical kind of machine sound real close to the chest instead of a heartbeat. This is constantly on, only audible real close to the chest.\nI have another sound on a gesture used for a facial gesture. The game object enabled, sound component disabled until I use it.\nNow, the model has a rotating arm cannon. And with avatar 3.0, I wanted to have it do a spool up sound on activation, a sustained spinning sound, and a wind down sound upon deactivation.\nto say nothing of the firing sound. Doing that, while having all the other sounds, was impossible and I had to abandon the idea and just have the spinning sound.\nYou may say \"just get rid of the always on sound\" but that's just my point, that I shouldn't need to.\nAvatar 3.0 makes it real easy to daisy chain sounds together for animations and toggles. Which with the 3 sound limit, becomes annoying to manage, as the limit is not very forgiving on overlaps. the 3 arm cannon sounds overlapped 1 to the other to the other, which on their own basically eat up the entire sound limit.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
